  "number": 5984,
  "title": "Add an internal CSS module theme context to useStyles(), shared by all packages",
  "body": "> Lets a theme style CSS Modules elements without readable class names.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\nNone: internal plumbing with no visible change, label `no-changelog`.\n\n## Description\n\nFluent can only style Web Chat elements through readable class names (`:global(.bubble)`). `useStyles()` now also adds the classes an internal `<CSSModuleThemeComposer>` above it provides for the same local name; without one, output is unchanged.\n\n## Design\n\n- Each package bundles its own copy of the styles package (own context), so bundle and Fluent now use the component's copy via `internal.js`, like `InjectStyleElements`; publishing the private package was the alternative.\n- The default `useStyles` transform keeps `<local> <hashed>`; `webChatPrefixedClassName` is ready for dropping plain names.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `styles/react`: `CSSModuleThemeContext`, `combineCSSModules()` (concatenates, frozen), `CSSModuleThemeComposer`, transforms, `useStyles()`\n- bundle cards, Fluent: shared copy, guarded by `no-restricted-imports`\n- unit specs for the above; `sharedStylesRuntime.spec.js`: one copy in the builds\n- typed with `CSSModuleTheme`: published typings check with `skipLibCheck: false`\n- `cssModuleTheme.fluent.html`: snapshot 1, a composer above Fluent outlines bubbles, Adaptive Card and send box\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
